WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.440 --> 00:00:02.340
Same data. Same settings.

2
00:00:02.503 --> 00:00:05.378
We only upgraded the software. What changed?

3
00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:11.353
The credible intervals of the space-time coefficients got much narrower.

4
00:00:11.770 --> 00:00:15.720
In plain terms: we can now say how much each factor matters,

5
00:00:15.707 --> 00:00:17.408
with far less uncertainty.

6
00:00:20.340 --> 00:00:22.077
First, two key terms.

7
00:00:22.240 --> 00:00:26.102
A regression coefficient tells you how much a factor affects the outcome.

8
00:00:26.530 --> 00:00:30.355
A credible interval is the range where that effect most likely lies.

9
00:00:30.780 --> 00:00:34.617
A forecast of 41 to 95 °F tells you nothing.

10
00:00:34.793 --> 00:00:37.680
64 to 72 °F, and you know what to wear.

11
00:00:38.110 --> 00:00:42.635
The narrower the range, the more certain the estimate, and the clearer the conclusion.

12
00:00:44.340 --> 00:00:46.827
We compared three public case studies:

13
00:00:46.852 --> 00:00:52.902
global healthy life expectancy, COVID-19 in China, and hepatitis B in the US.

14
00:00:53.065 --> 00:00:57.690
We ran each one in both versions and measured how wide the intervals were.

15
00:01:00.340 --> 00:01:05.128
First, temporal coefficients: how a factor's effect changes from year to year.

16
00:01:05.328 --> 00:01:12.990
Global healthy life expectancy: 99% narrower, just 1/69 of the original width.

17
00:01:14.340 --> 00:01:20.040
COVID-19 in China: 94% narrower, 1/16 of the width.

18
00:01:22.340 --> 00:01:27.690
Hepatitis B in the US: 99% narrower, 1/100 of the width.

19
00:01:30.240 --> 00:01:35.202
3 cases, 22 predictors, 372 temporal intervals.

20
00:01:35.365 --> 00:01:37.127
Every single one got narrower.

21
00:01:40.340 --> 00:01:45.615
Next, spatial coefficients: how the same factor's effect differs from place to place.

22
00:01:48.240 --> 00:01:52.127
Global healthy life expectancy: 38% narrower.

23
00:01:52.290 --> 00:01:55.503
Every country that shares a border got narrower intervals.

24
00:01:58.340 --> 00:02:02.490
COVID-19 in China: 87% narrower.

25
00:02:04.340 --> 00:02:08.190
Hepatitis B in the US: 98% narrower.

26
00:02:10.340 --> 00:02:11.303
Here's the summary.

27
00:02:11.465 --> 00:02:15.490
Temporal coefficients: intervals more than 90% narrower.

28
00:02:15.653 --> 00:02:19.640
Spatial coefficients: 38–98% narrower.

29
00:02:19.802 --> 00:02:22.240
Model fit: on par with the old version.

30
00:02:22.720 --> 00:02:26.695
In short: more certain estimates, with no loss in model fit.

31
00:02:28.340 --> 00:02:31.852
BSTVC. Making space and time explainable.

32
00:02:32.270 --> 00:02:34.820
Narrower intervals. Clearer conclusions.

33
00:02:36.440 --> 00:02:41.590
BSTVC Desktop V2 is free to download for research. No coding needed.

34
00:02:41.753 --> 00:02:45.715
Scan the code, or visit the BSTVC homepage to get started.
